		Funny, the thing that drags people off and dumps them in the treeline, and he can't so much as lift his head off the floorboards now. You roll him onto his back with one boot to look at him properly.
		<br>
		<<thought>>Wraith. Beat you and you don't wake up at home, you come to out past the forest road with rope on your wrists and a long walk ahead. The mean one. The one I planned for.<</thought>>
		<br>
		<<mc>>No woods for me tonight. You're the one not going anywhere.<</mc>>
		<br>
		You're loose and reckless on the back of it, and the want creeping up surprises you more than the win does.
	<<case "Mare">>
		He's spread on his back where your bedroom floor would be if this were home, arms gone slack, the fight finally out of him after how many nights he crept in to make it worse.
		<br>
		<<mc>>Hello, you. The bedroom one.<</mc>>
		<br>
		<<thought>>The only haunt with the nerve to follow a girl to her own pillow and turn meaner every dawn. Holy water on the floorboards would've sent him packing; instead I got him on the floorboards. He'd have given up in a few days regardless, but this is faster.<</thought>>
		<br>
		You lean down close enough to smell the cold off his skin and feel your own pulse answer, which is the wrong response to a thing that haunts your sleep, and you know it, and you don't move.
	<<case "Cthulion">>
		He's wearing the human face still, the borrowed one, slumped back against the baseboard looking almost ordinary except for the limbs that didn't fully draw back in, two of them lying boneless across the floor where he reached for you.
		<br>
		<<mc>>There you are. There's the thing under the nice face.<</mc>>
		<br>
		A Cthulion keeps that stolen shape on like a coat until it actually wants you, and then it stops being shy and reaches — older than the whole species, wearing one of us, undone on the floor of a rental house.
		<br>
		<<thought>>I have personally fucked a thing too old to have a real shape into lying still, and the smart, sane response to that is horror. I'll get to the horror. Give me a second. I'm still a little hot about the reaching.<</thought>>
	<<case "Banshee">>
		Her mouth is the part you keep watching, slack and harmless now, the same mouth that came at you earlier and lifted ten clean points off your sanity in one go. You crouch close, careful, the way you'd lean over a wasp you're fairly sure is dead.
		<br>
		<<thought>>Banshee. The only girl in the catalogue, and the whole act is the kiss. One press of that and you're down ten before you've finished flinching.<</thought>>
		<br>
		<<mc>>All that fuss over a kiss. You're pretty when you're not robbing me.<</mc>>
		<br>
		Your chest is doing something warm and unhelpful, and the safest reading is that you're glad she's spent, so you go with that one.
	<<case "Raiju">>
		He's draped over your gear bag with one thigh hooked across the EMF reader, the screen under him still throwing junk numbers, your thermometer beside it reading a cheerful lie.
		<br>
		<<mc>>Have a look at the artist.<</mc>>
		<br>
		<<thought>>The Raiju bled into all of it — made the EMF spike at nothing, the temp gauge fib, the Spirit Box answer me in pure hiss where the others would've spoken. Every tool I own corrupted right when I'd need it. And here he is, pulse glitching, twitching off my hardware like he can't stop charging it.<</thought>>
		<br>
		You're grinning and you're soaked and you genuinely could not tell him how much of what just happened was real, which is exactly his trick, and exactly why you'll do it again. Crikey.
	<<default>>
		<<mc>>And this beauty — no idea. Never logged one with this exact set of tells.<</mc>>
		<br>
		<<thought>>You tilt your head at it the way you'd tilt it at a snake you couldn't key out. Whatever it is, it built itself to take exactly what it just gave you, and it did the work without once asking your opinion. Gorgeous. Filthy. Going in the notebook the second your hands stop shaking.<</thought>>
	<</switch>><br>
	<<mc>>Right. Off you pop.<</mc>>
	<br>
	<<thought>>You stand, knees complaining, and the host voice goes back wherever it lives. The EMF's still in your other hand. Still a house to clear, still a thing to find, and you are absolutely not getting paid to narrate.<</thought>><br>
<</widget>>
